  "problem": "HRSA AHRF, NPPES, SAMHSA, T-MSIS/TAF and SVI lacked evidence-backed intake dispositions. TAF restricted research files could be confused with public Medicaid summary products. Adding a route could assert access to restricted TAF data. Unsupported protocols could become unbounded scrapers. ASPE catalog SVI could be treated as ATSDR SVI. Synar tables could satisfy SAMHSA facility services. NPI could be treated as CCN. Catalog membership could be invented. Frozen named-source-registry.v1.0.0.json or connector src could be edited.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Federal intake lives in packages/connectors/source-registry/ with five frozen family records. Every locator is publisher-supported. TAF restricted research files are not public Medicaid summaries, and adding a route never asserts TAF access. Each family has a literal configuration and fixture. An unsupported protocol produces a specific extension task rather than a scraper. Original NPPES/AHRF/SAMHSA/SVI questions identify the intended family; ASPE catalog record ypqf-r5qs is not ATSDR SVI. Catalog membership is not invented. Frozen packages/retrieval/fixtures/named-source-registry.v1.0.0.json (9748 bytes) and packages/connectors/src are unchanged. Last-good generation live-2026-09-03-85b50522b420 is unchanged.",
